-- title:
--   Deterministic filtering: from a modular counting oracle to All-Edges Exact Triangle
-- statement:
--   For every program $P$ whose procedure $p_o$ solves the counting oracle task `oracleTask` within $T_o$ steps with need $\nu_o$, there are procedures $R$ and an index $p'$ such that procedure $p'$ of $P\mathbin{+\!\!+}R$ solves All-Edges Exact Triangle (`aeTask`: for each pair $(a,b)$ of an $n$-vertex instance with weights bounded by $U$, the flag whether some $c$ has $w(a,b)+w(b,c)+w(a,c)=0$) within `filterTime To n U` steps and with need `filterNeed νo n U`; and `filterNeed νo` is polynomially bounded whenever $\nu_o$ is.
--
--   `filterTime` is the time of the host: computing the parameters, a sieve for the prime pool in $[R,2R)$, the marks, and `roundsOf n` rounds of `rOf n` steps, each step calling the oracle once per pool prime and each round twice more, every call within the largest oracle time over the moduli up to $P_{\max}=(2R)^r$; then the final answer (the certified flags under the guard, or a scan of the remaining candidates).
-- source:
--   Developed for the prove2.me APSP exponent campaign (https://prove2.me/campaigns/apsp-exponent) on top of the Lean formalization anthropics/formal-math, folder 3sum-apsp, commit e1a4e65 (https://github.com/anthropics/formal-math/tree/e1a4e6508154ea59f030480661590a9fe3018011/3sum-apsp; Lean v4.33.1, Mathlib v4.33.1). The statement comes from the file 3sum-apsp/ThreeSumApsp/Filter/HostMain.lean of the campaign's modified copy of that library, which is not published; the new definitions it uses are in the platform definition bundles APSP2996001_Defs1 and APSP2996001_Defs2 (and APSP299791_Defs1 to APSP299791_Defs5 of the 2.99791 entry). It follows the technical note "Deterministic APSP via thin products" (6 October 2026) refining J. Alman and V. Vassilevska Williams, "Truly Subquadratic 3SUM and Truly Subcubic APSP via Triangles in Sparse Lopsided Graphs", arXiv:2610.06783v1 (https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.06783v1), Lemma 3.1 and Section 3.

